title: Kubeconfig default warns and builds "/.kube/config" when HOME is unset
updated: 2026-08-13T17:35:18Z
---

Kubeconfig.pm:68 reads

    default => sub { $ENV{KUBECONFIG} // "$ENV{HOME}/.kube/config" },

With HOME unset and KUBECONFIG unset the interpolation of undef warns ("Use of uninitialized value $ENV{\"HOME\"} in concatenation") and then produces the path "/.kube/config", so the eventual error is "Cannot open /.kube/config: No such file or directory" rather than anything naming the real problem. HOME is genuinely unset in cron jobs, some systemd units and minimal containers -- exactly where a missing kubeconfig is hardest to read off a stack trace.

The same expression used to sit in CLI::Role::Connection as the option default too; #8 removed that copy, so this is now the only one left, but it is a pre-existing line that #8 did not touch.

Fix is to croak with something like "Cannot determine kubeconfig path: neither KUBECONFIG nor HOME is set" instead of interpolating undef. That changes the failure mode of a currently-warning path, so it wants a Changes bullet, and t/14_kubeconfig.t should pin it with a local delete of both variables.
